WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.040
Let’s look at the ankles, and the middle of the foot.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.310
The ankle and the middle of the foot can become inflamed.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.440
This can cause pain, and make walking harder.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.780
This is different from pain where a tendon joins the heel bone.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.370
The feet and heel lesson covers those spots.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:28.810
Use the map to show where the problem is: around the ankle, across the middle of the foot, or at the heel.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.790
Mention when it began, and any change in walking.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.720
The location helps guide an exam.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.930
But it does not show the cause by itself.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.790
Physical therapists help improve joint function.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.400
Occupational therapists teach ways to protect your joints, and save energy.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.470
Great job! Let’s review.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.040
Pain or swelling here can make walking harder.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.030
It does not show the cause by itself.
